  "description": "The archetype of the American city commuter bike, The Dash is designed for daily transportation. Made in Chicago by Heritage Bikes and Coffee.\n\nConceptualized by Taylor Stitch, Aaron Stinner of Stinner Bicycles developed the geometry with the utilitarian in mind;\n\nHooded paragon dropouts make aligning the axle a pleasurable experience, fixed or freewheel.\n\nThe Dash can be fitted with hand operated caliper brakes, or enjoy the old-school feel of a coaster brake.\n\nWith a hand built frame and wheels, and sealed bearings used throughout, your Heritage is built for longevity.",
